cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hands-On AI Security"
message: >-
  If you use this work — the book, the code, or the attack corpus — please
  cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jajoo
    given-names: Sanskar
repository-code: "https://github.com/m4vic/Hands-On-Ai-Security"
abstract: >-
  A builder's course in AI security. You build an attacker, a defender and a
  target — three small systems that grow up together — and learn by breaking
  and fixing your own machines rather than reading about someone else's.
  Every claim in the work is backed by code that was actually written and
  actually run: measured results, not assurances.
keywords:
